*Heading
 An explicit step without output requests: Abaqus' default output at 20 intervals
** abq2ccx example: no *Output request at all, so Abaqus/Explicit writes its preselected
** field output at 20 equal intervals of the step.  ccx ignores *TIME POINTS in explicit
** dynamics and would write every increment; abq2ccx gives the output cards a FREQUENCY
** from the increment ccx will take, its own Courant estimate (8.85e-7 s here).
** Steel bar 10 x 10 x 200 (20 C3D8), x = 0 held along x, moving at v0 = -1000 mm/s
** (towards the support) when the step starts.  The support sends a wave up the bar at
** c = sqrt(E / rho) = 5.172e6 mm/s; the free end keeps moving at v0 until the wave
** arrives at t = L / c = 3.867e-5 s, then moves back: u_x(tip, L / c) = v0 L / c =
** -0.038668.  The step lasts 2 L / c.
